.TH rc-keeper-add 1  "rc-keeper-add " 
.SH NAME
rc\-keeper\-add \- Add a folder as a new instance
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBrc\-keeper\-add\fR [\fB\-\-name\fR] [\fB\-\-chrome\fR] [\fB\-\-no\-chrome\fR] [\fB\-\-permission\-mode\fR] [\fB\-\-spawn\fR] [\fB\-\-capacity\fR] [\fB\-\-create\-session\-in\-dir\fR] [\fB\-\-no\-create\-session\-in\-dir\fR] [\fB\-\-session\-name\-prefix\fR] [\fB\-\-auto\-trust\fR] [\fB\-\-no\-auto\-trust\fR] [\fB\-\-auto\-start\fR] [\fB\-\-no\-auto\-start\fR] [\fB\-\-force\-boot\fR] [\fB\-\-no\-force\-boot\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] <\fIFOLDER\fR> [\fIEXTRA_ARGS\fR] 
.SH DESCRIPTION
Add a folder as a new instance
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-name\fR \fI<NAME>\fR
Session name shown in Claude. Passed as `claude remote\-control \-\-name`. Not set by default
.TP
\fB\-\-chrome\fR
Start with Chrome integration. Passed as `\-\-chrome`. On by default for `add`
.TP
\fB\-\-no\-chrome\fR
Start without Chrome integration. Passed as `\-\-no\-chrome`. Turns off the `add` default
.TP
\fB\-\-permission\-mode\fR \fI<PERMISSION_MODE>\fR
Permission mode. Passed as `\-\-permission\-mode`. One of: acceptEdits, auto, bypassPermissions, default, dontAsk, plan. Not set by default, so `claude` decides
.br

.br
\fIPossible values:\fR
.RS 14
.IP \(bu 2
acceptEdits
.IP \(bu 2
auto
.IP \(bu 2
bypassPermissions
.IP \(bu 2
default
.IP \(bu 2
dontAsk
.IP \(bu 2
plan
.RE
.TP
\fB\-\-spawn\fR \fI<SPAWN>\fR
Session spawn mode. Passed as `\-\-spawn`. One of: same\-dir, worktree, session. Not set by default
.br

.br
\fIPossible values:\fR
.RS 14
.IP \(bu 2
same\-dir
.IP \(bu 2
worktree
.IP \(bu 2
session
.RE
.TP
\fB\-\-capacity\fR \fI<CAPACITY>\fR
Maximum number of sessions. Passed as `\-\-capacity`. Whole number. Not set by default
.TP
\fB\-\-create\-session\-in\-dir\fR
Create sessions in the instance folder. Passed as `\-\-create\-session\-in\-dir`. Not set by default
.TP
\fB\-\-no\-create\-session\-in\-dir\fR
Do not create sessions in the instance folder. Passed as `\-\-no\-create\-session\-in\-dir`
.TP
\fB\-\-session\-name\-prefix\fR \fI<SESSION_NAME_PREFIX>\fR
Prefix for remote session names. Passed as `\-\-remote\-control\-session\-name\-prefix`. Not set by default
.TP
\fB\-\-auto\-trust\fR
Answer the folder trust prompt for this instance. On by default for `add`. Not passed to `claude`
.TP
\fB\-\-no\-auto\-trust\fR
Do not answer the folder trust prompt. You must trust the folder yourself. Not passed to `claude`
.TP
\fB\-\-auto\-start\fR
Start this instance now and each time the daemon starts. On by default for `add`. Not passed to `claude`
.TP
\fB\-\-no\-auto\-start\fR
Do not start this instance with the daemon. Start it with `rc\-keeper start`. Not passed to `claude`
.TP
\fB\-\-force\-boot\fR
When another `claude remote\-control` serves the folder, stop it and start this instance. Kills without asking. Not passed to `claude`
.TP
\fB\-\-no\-force\-boot\fR
Back off when the folder is busy instead of taking it over. Off by default. Not passed to `claude`
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help
.TP
<\fIFOLDER\fR>
Folder that `claude remote\-control` runs in. Must exist. Stored as an absolute path
.TP
[\fIEXTRA_ARGS\fR]
Extra arguments for `claude remote\-control`. Add them after `\-\-`, e.g. `add DIR \-\- \-\-verbose`
